-- An input of a section GIVEN, in a slot. A rule under the section reads the
-- section's inputs as its own, so an input of a built-in type in a slot of a
-- mixfix pattern or an @nlg sentence reads as a blank, "[income]", as a rule's
-- own input does (legalese/l4-ide#803). Before, it read as a bare name beside
-- the pattern's words, "income reduced by 10".

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      cut IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
amount `reduced by` cut MEANS amount MINUS cut

§ `Eligibility`
    GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
          income IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`net income` MEANS income `reduced by` 10

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %x% is above the age
`above` x MEANS x > age

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`check` MEANS `above` income

#EVAL `check` WITH age IS 20, income IS 30
